WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.880 --> 00:00:09.660
This is a song that was written to a track that's a Loop that was made with the sounds that I made with my mouth.

00:00:11.160 --> 00:00:12.680
Good morning, John.

00:00:13.660 --> 00:00:19.720
If I had a dollar bill, I would give a piece to everyone.

00:00:19.760 --> 00:00:26.000
There's a hole I wanna fill that gets smaller every song that's sung.

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:37.660
Cause when I make a meal, or when I kiss a girl, well this might sound a bit surreal, but that's me giving to the world.

00:00:37.660 --> 00:00:39.780
I wanna buy the world a coke.

00:00:40.620 --> 00:00:43.860
I'd do better telling you to eat your wheaties.

00:00:43.860 --> 00:00:45.860
I wanna sing a song.

00:00:46.580 --> 00:00:50.220
I don't wanna give you type two diabetes.

00:00:50.220 --> 00:00:55.780
So when you party hard, or when you go to the bank,

00:00:55.780 --> 00:01:03.700
or when you mow the yard, or you name your new son Hank, well you're moving it along.

00:01:04.300 --> 00:01:07.880
This is the method that drives the whole thing forward.

00:01:07.880 --> 00:01:09.880
It's possible I'm wrong,

00:01:10.520 --> 00:01:14.100
but I think that praise is absolutely unheard.

00:01:14.100 --> 00:01:19.920
There's so much that must be done and so many folks to do it.

00:01:20.240 --> 00:01:25.700
And I know sometimes it's hard, but together we get through it.

00:01:25.700 --> 00:01:30.820
No one does it all alone, nobody does it all alone.

00:01:31.500 --> 00:01:36.980
Nobody does it all aloooooone, nobody does it all alone.

00:01:43.360 --> 00:01:49.440
If I had a dollar bill, I would give a piece to everyone.

00:01:49.440 --> 00:01:55.740
There's a hole I wanna fill that gets smaller every song that's sung

00:02:06.240 --> 00:02:10.640
Thank you to the hundreds of people who created beats using that sounds that I made with my mouth at star.me.

00:02:10.640 --> 00:02:14.040
You can still go and beatbox with me, at star.me, if you want to, the link is in the description.

00:02:14.040 --> 00:02:17.180
But there was, like, so much of this going on in that video.

00:02:17.180 --> 00:02:22.560
I just wanted to do something different and it's black and white because I didn't want you to see the natural colour of my teeth.

00:02:23.040 --> 00:02:23.540
Honesty!

00:02:23.680 --> 00:02:28.060
So John, that song that I just sang for you and everyone else is about not being special.

00:02:28.060 --> 00:02:34.860
And it's about how not being special is not only, like, really normal, it's also really necessary and really wonderful.

00:02:34.860 --> 00:02:39.660
All of the normal things that we do every day, taking care of our kids and emptying out septic tanks

00:02:39.660 --> 00:02:43.180
and learning things and having fun and being silly,

00:02:43.180 --> 00:02:45.540
those are the things that make the world work.

00:02:45.540 --> 00:02:51.280
On the other hand, Steve Jobs, one of the most special people of his generation and one of my personal heroes just died a couple of days ago.

00:02:51.280 --> 00:02:54.380
And that of course reminds us all how important people like that are.

00:02:54.380 --> 00:02:58.960
It's always a little bit dangerous to talk about someone right after they died because we tend to, like, inflate their importance,

00:02:58.960 --> 00:03:03.140
but it's kind of difficult for me to imagine inflating the importance of Steve Jobs.

00:03:03.140 --> 00:03:05.140
He made what we do possible, John.

00:03:05.140 --> 00:03:07.880
From our first computer, the Apple II e that Dad got,

00:03:07.880 --> 00:03:12.040
all the way to the computers that we got in 2007 to get ready for this project

00:03:12.040 --> 00:03:16.740
and all of the software that we've ever edited any video on: that was all because of Steve Jobs.

00:03:16.740 --> 00:03:22.900
John, we are in the very not-unique situation of having a job that depended on Steve Jobs existence.

00:03:22.900 --> 00:03:27.360
I didn't know Steve Jobs, I don't know what kind of guy he was, I just know him through the things that he created.

00:03:27.360 --> 00:03:32.060
And because of the things that he created, he was important to me and he made my life better

00:03:32.080 --> 00:03:34.020
and I think that the world is less good without him.

00:03:34.020 --> 00:03:36.020
And maybe that's what we should be trying for in the end.

00:03:36.020 --> 00:03:39.780
For, at the end of our lives, for the world to be less good without us.

00:03:39.780 --> 00:03:43.100
And if that's the case, maybe we don't have to be special to be like Steve Jobs,

00:03:43.100 --> 00:03:45.300
maybe we just have to be good.

00:03:45.300 --> 00:03:47.600
John, I'll see you on Monday.

